div.p:
It is the desire and intention of the Federal Republic not to build a military machine or to develop its economic capacity for military production beyond its agreed contribution to the European Defence Community. Acting in accordance with its powers under Article 26(2) of the Basic Law, the Federal Government will not permit the production on Federal territory of the materials listed below, and will take all suitable steps to forbid scientific research devoted to the development of models and the construction of equipment specifically designed for the production of the materials in question, [except as
may be requested by the European Defence Commissioners in the interests of Western Defence (United States/United Kingdom)]:—
atomic, biological and chemical weapons;
long range and guided missiles;
aircraft [including civil aircraft (France/United Kingdom)];
naval vessels other than minor defensive craft;
[propellents and gun barrels of more than 105 mm (France)]
